    "title": "How withdrawals work",
    "blocks": [
      {
        "type": "quote",
        "text": "**Level:** Beginner → Intermediate · **Read time:** 9 min"
      },
      {
        "type": "p",
        "text": "Withdrawal behaviour **depends on the vault**. The vault page in the Concrete app says which model applies. There are three."
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "level": 2,
        "text": "1. Atomic vault - instant"
      },
      {
        "type": "p",
        "text": "`withdraw()` / `redeem()` deallocates from strategies (in a configured order), burns your shares and sends assets in **one transaction**. Suits strategies whose liquidity is always available on-chain."
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "level": 2,
        "text": "2. Queued withdrawal vault - epochs (most common)"
      },
      {
        "type": "p",
        "text": "Used where strategies involve off-chain custody or slower unwinds."
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "lang": "",
        "code": "Request ──► Epoch collects requests ──► Cutoff ──► Process ──► Claim\n (shares       (you may cancel             (locked)   (price fixed,   (assets\n  held by       until cutoff)                          shares burned,  arrive in\n  vault)                                               assets reserved) wallet)"
      },
      {
        "type": "ol",
        "items": [
          "**Submit** on the vault's Withdraw tab. Your shares are held by the vault and join the current epoch.",
          "**Cutoff.** The epoch closes at a scheduled time. Cancel only before it; after that you are locked in and a new epoch opens.",
          "**Process.** Shortly after the cutoff, the **share price is locked at processing time** (not request time), shares are burned and assets are reserved - first from idle balance, then by the Allocator deallocating from strategies.",
          "**Claim.** Status moves **Queued → Processing → Available**; click Claim. Several ready epochs can be claimed together."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "level": 3,
        "text": "Withdrawal caps"
      },
      {
        "type": "p",
        "text": "Some vaults limit each epoch to a **percentage of TVL**. If requests exceed the cap, the remainder rolls to later epochs in **FIFO** order, and you keep earning until your portion is processed."
      },
      {
        "type": "p",
        "text": "*Example (from the docs' pattern):* weekly processing, 20% cap. A request submitted on a Friday joins the next Tuesday's epoch; if under the cap, funds are claimable a few days later. If over the cap, you're served in submission order across later epochs."
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "level": 3,
        "text": "Cooldowns"
      },
      {
        "type": "p",
        "text": "Some vaults add a **withdrawal cooldown**: shares from each deposit only become withdrawable/transferable after that deposit's cooldown ends (each deposit has its own clock). Early exit, where allowed, may cost a fee paid in shares (0-1%, decaying toward expiry). Cooldown applies *in addition to* queues and caps."
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "level": 3,
        "text": "Things to know"
      },
      {
        "type": "ul",
        "items": [
          "Not instant: expect a delay set by epoch cadence + unwind time (the WBTC vault card showed a 21-day queue at snapshot time).",
          "Final amount = share price **at processing**, so it can move between request and settlement.",
          "Each vault has minimum and maximum withdrawal sizes.",
          "Requests can roll over when caps bind or processing is delayed."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "level": 2,
        "text": "3. Pre-deposit (cross-chain) vault - claim, not queue"
      },
      {
        "type": "p",
        "text": "Used for launch campaigns: you deposit on a source chain, the vault locks, assets bridge to the target chain, and you **claim** shares there through LayerZero messaging. You need control of the same address on the destination chain and enough native token on the source chain for the fee. See [Campaigns & pre-deposits](/docs/02-intermediate/04-campaigns-and-predeposits)."
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Priority withdrawals (advanced footnote)"
      },
      {
        "type": "p",
        "text": "Async vaults have a privileged `PRIORITY_WITHDRAWAL_EXECUTOR` that can fast-track a payout against the active epoch at `grossAssets − unwindCost`, with `unwindCost` capped by an admin setting (default 500 bps, ceiling 10,000 bps). It is a trusted operational role, not an automatic user feature. See [Async withdrawals deep dive](/docs/03-advanced/03-async-withdrawals-deep-dive)."
      },
      {
        "type": "p",
        "text": "Next: [06 · Fees](/docs/01-beginner/06-fees)."
      }
    ]
